
# --- GOLDEN TEST FIXTURE (2026-09-20) ---
# resetMode=loadvm: reset the guest between tests with QMP 'loadvm golden'.
# Fixture = Linux 0.12 at its root shell, with the whole 1992 boot still on
# screen above the prompt:
#   Loading.......................
#   Press <RETURN> to see SVGA-modes available or any other key to continue.
#   8 virtual consoles / 4 pty's
#   Partition tables ok.
#   Swap device ok: 1023 pages (4190208 bytes) swap-space
#   6/1440 free blocks / 408/480 free inodes
#   3369 buffers = 3449856 bytes buffer space
#   Free mem: 12582912 bytes
#     Ok.
#   [/usr/root]#
# That banner is a one-shot: it scrolls away the moment a visitor types enough
# lines, and a cold boot stops at the SVGA-mode prompt waiting for a keypress.
# The golden therefore captures the scene deliberately, right after boot, so
# every reset returns the visitor to it.
# Text console, no pointer surface (SH_POINTER=none) — Linux 0.12 has no mouse
# driver of any kind.
#
# Golden baked with the SAME device set as qemu-streamhost.sh (rule 6): boot
# from the kernel floppy, root from IDE master partition 1, blank IDE slave
# present, CHS 64/16/32 on both, -m 16 -smp 1, -vga std, KVM, no NIC.
# The slave disk is part of the device set, not an accident — see the launcher.
# Keyboard pacing: fleet floor 40/40.
# AUDIO: PC speaker only (kernel/chr_drv/console.c sysbeep); no sound card.
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=linux012-root-shell-boot-banner
